# {{.AppName}}

A multi-stack Lift application using Pay Theory-style deployment.

## Project Structure

```
{{.AppName}}/
├── cmd/
│   ├── api/            # API Lambda entrypoint
│   └── worker/         # Worker Lambda entrypoint
├── cdk/                # CDK infrastructure (data + service stacks)
├── dist/               # Build outputs (generated)
├── shell/              # Deployment scripts
│   ├── build.sh
│   ├── deploy.sh
│   └── init_env_vars.sh
├── buildspec.yml       # CodeBuild specification
└── lift.yaml           # Lift project configuration
```

## Quick Start

```bash
# Initialize environment (edit PARTNER first)
source ./shell/init_env_vars.sh

# Build Lambda functions
./shell/build.sh

# Deploy both stacks to dev
./shell/deploy.sh --partner <partner> --stage dev
```

## Deploy Options

```bash
# Deploy all stacks (data then service)
./shell/deploy.sh --partner mypartner --stage dev --stack --all

# Deploy only data stack
./shell/deploy.sh --partner mypartner --stage dev --stack data

# Deploy only service stack (requires data stack already deployed)
./shell/deploy.sh --partner mypartner --stage dev --stack service
```

## Using Lift CLI

```bash
lift build
lift up --stage dev --partner mypartner
```

## Stack Naming

Stacks are named with the pattern:

- `{{.AppName}}-data-<partner>-<stage>`
- `{{.AppName}}-service-<partner>-<stage>`

Example:

- `{{.AppName}}-data-mypartner-dev`
- `{{.AppName}}-service-mypartner-dev`

